From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 20:47:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: npu: publish mailbox command before doorbell

airoha_npu_send_msg() currently increments MBQ0_CTRL2 before writing the
command flags to MBQ0_CTRL3. The firmware treats the CTRL2 producer index
update as a doorbell, so it can consume the previous CTRL3 contents before
the host publishes the new function ID and WAIT_RSP bit.

This can make a request complete with stale status and response data. On
AN7581 with the MT7996 firmware it is visible during probe as firmware
version 0.0, followed by rejected PPE and WLAN offload setup requests.

Match the Airoha SDK mailbox protocol and write CTRL3 before incrementing
CTRL2. Ordered MMIO writes then make the complete request visible before
the firmware is notified.

Fixes: 23290c7bc190 ("net: airoha: Introduce Airoha NPU support")
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
@@ -198,10 +198,10 @@ static int __airoha_npu_send_msg(struct
 
 	regmap_write(npu->regmap, REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(0) + offset, core->addr);
 	regmap_write(npu->regmap, REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(1) + offset, len);
-	regmap_read(npu->regmap, REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(2) + offset, &val);
-	regmap_write(npu->regmap, REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(2) + offset, val + 1);
 	val = FIELD_PREP(MBOX_MSG_FUNC_ID, func_id) | MBOX_MSG_WAIT_RSP;
 	regmap_write(npu->regmap, REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(3) + offset, val);
+	regmap_read(npu->regmap, REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(2) + offset, &val);
+	regmap_write(npu->regmap, REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(2) + offset, val + 1);
 
 	ret = regmap_read_poll_timeout_atomic(npu->regmap,
 					      REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(3) + offset,
